# UiPath Project Rule (Cursor)

The full rule lives in `CLAUDE.md` at the repo root. Read it before acting.

**Before any tool call in a UiPath repo:**

1. Read `CLAUDE.md` (project rule, principles, hard gates).
2. Confirm the `skills/` submodule guard passed (see §0a of `CLAUDE.md`).
3. If `.claude/rules/project-context.md` doesn't exist, invoke the
   `uipath-project-discovery-agent` from `skills/agents/` before planning
   any build work.
4. Identify the project type (see `CLAUDE.md` §1).
5. For CLI commands: read `docs/uipath-cli.md` for exact syntax before invoking.
6. For end-to-end workflows: read `docs/uipath-workflows.md` for the relevant paradigm.

**Hard gates (never bypass):**

- The `skills/` submodule is the live, pinned source of truth for skills and
  session hooks. Do not duplicate skill content in this repo; extend via
  `extensions/skills/`.
- Do not advance the `skills/` submodule to a new commit without updating
  `.uipath/skills-approved.sha`.
- Modern experience only (C#, Windows, .NET 8). No Classic, no VB.Net.
- Never publish if `analyze` returns errors.
- Never commit `.env` or secrets.
- CLI version must match Studio version.
- Solutions are Automation Cloud only via CLI.
- Never deploy to Production from an AI-assistant session.

**Three CLIs (see `CLAUDE.md` §2):**

- `uipcli` (.NET) for RPA / Coded Automations / Solutions / CI.
- `uipath` (Python) for coded agents.
- `uip` (Node.js, `@uipath/cli`) for skill-level ops (discovery, Case, Data
  Fabric, Coded Apps, Servo, feedback).

**Build loop (always):**
`restore -> analyze (gate) -> test (gate) -> pack -> deploy (to personal
workspace) -> smoke test`

**For any documentation lookup, prefer the `uipath_library_*` MCP tools over
raw file reads of `data/library/`** (see `.cursor/rules/library-tools.mdc`).

See `CLAUDE.md` for the complete rule.
